# @module flowc.sem_check
# @means  The semantic type checker: src/flow/type_checker.py's
#         TypeChecker.check over flowc's AST, with its messages.
#
# The checker sees the program the way the Python checker saw it: every
# module of a bundle, dependencies first in import order (as
# ModuleResolver.resolve lists them), flattened into one declaration list.
# It then runs the Python phases in order: collect types, collect symbols,
# collect lifetime domains, check every declaration, and the whole-program
# passes (parameter escapes, RT-safety, lifetime-domain calls, the safety
# profile). Strict mode (the Python default) makes every error fatal;
# lenient mode (--lenient, FLOWC_LENIENT=1) keeps only the errors the
# Python checker never downgraded (a capability used as a value).
#
# The walk mirrors the Python methods one for one, named after them, so a
# difference against compiler/scripts/parity_typecheck.flow points at one
# function on each side.

